The AMDGPU plugin is ordinary HSA host code and its sources already carry
non-x86 fallbacks (offload/plugins-nextgen/amdgpu/src/rtl.cpp guards the
synchronous-copy paths with __i386__/__x86_64__), but the plugin gate in
offload/CMakeLists.txt only whitelists x86_64/ppc64le/aarch64/riscv64 hosts.
On loongarch64 the requested plugin is therefore dropped from
LIBOMPTARGET_PLUGINS_TO_BUILD and the built libomptarget supports offloading
to the host only.

--- a/offload/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/offload/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -194,7 +194,7 @@
 list(APPEND LIBOMPTARGET_PLUGINS_TO_BUILD "host")
 list(REMOVE_DUPLICATES LIBOMPTARGET_PLUGINS_TO_BUILD)
 
-if(NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "(x86_64)|(ppc64le)|(aarch64)|(riscv64)$"
+if(NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "(x86_64)|(ppc64le)|(aarch64)|(riscv64)|(loongarch64)$"
         AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux"))
   if("amdgpu" IN_LIST LIBOMPTARGET_PLUGINS_TO_BUILD)
     message(STATUS "Not building AMDGPU plugin: only support AMDGPU in "
